  46 guard-valid stage-1 designs across 16 specs; 19 of them sit below the band

  where each population sits, in unit design coordinates:
  axis     calibration set (n=8)  PPO low-peak (n=19)    inside
  w_in     0.512 - 0.981          0.213 - 0.973          17/19
  l_in     0.012 - 0.987          0.082 - 0.993          18/19  <-- repair coordinate
  i_tail   0.005 - 0.760          0.069 - 0.759          19/19
  rs       0.057 - 0.896          0.233 - 0.773          19/19  <-- repair coordinate
  cs       0.436 - 0.866          0.289 - 1.000          16/19
  r_load   0.249 - 0.980          0.467 - 0.982          18/19

  jointly on the two repair coordinates (rs, l_in): 18 of 19 PPO low-peak designs
  fall inside the calibration set's box
  a design outside that box is not necessarily mis-served -- it means the probe did not
  measure there, so the plane's behaviour at that point is an extrapolation the same way
  the high-peak plane was below the band.

